# Rules for the archive EAS Build uploads to its build workers, for builds run from this expo/ folder.
#
# Why this file exists: EAS CLI archives the project by copying every file except those matched by
# .gitignore — and .gitignore in this folder ignores google-services.json, the Firebase Android
# config CI writes from the FIREBASE_GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON secret. Ignored means "not uploaded", so
# the worker would receive a project whose app.json points at a file that is not there, and the
# build fails before it compiles anything. Once .easignore exists it is used INSTEAD OF .gitignore,
# so every secret rule from .gitignore is restated here. The one deliberate difference is that
# google-services.json is NOT listed: it stays out of Git but still reaches the build worker.
# Source: https://expo.fyi/eas-build-archive
#
#   *** KEEP THIS FILE IN STEP WITH expo/.gitignore ***

node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
.env
.env.*
*.log
.DS_Store
ios
android
.claude/preflight-logs/

# Credentials that must never be uploaded. The Play service-account key is uploaded to EAS
# separately (eas credentials) — it is not part of the build archive.
credentials/
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p8
google-service-account*.json
play-service-account*.json
